# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit. cookies.txt is a Netscape cookie jar holding live
# YouTube session tokens (SID, SAPISID, __Secure-*PSID, LOGIN_INFO); leaking it
# is an account takeover, not just a lost login. If it ever lands in a commit,
# sign out of YouTube everywhere to revoke the session, then rewrite history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cookies.txt
*cookies*
.env
*.token
*.key
*credentials*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored binary (~38 MB). Deliberately not committed: ./yy.zsh -U rewrites it
# in place, so every update would add another 38 MB blob to history forever.
# See README.md for how to fetch it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
yt-dlp
yt-dlp.exe

# Optional local media/runtime tools. Large machine-specific binaries.
deno.exe
ffmpeg.exe
ffplay.exe
ffprobe.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state and personal viewing history — local to each machine.
# channel-ids.txt is a subscription list: it names exactly who the maintainer
# follows, which is not something to publish from a public repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
current_url.txt
current_url.json
checkpoint.txt
channel-check-status.json
downloaded-videos.json
html-video-cache.json
html-video-cache.tsv
channel-id-cache.txt
channel-ids.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Disposable runtime files: self-update staging and backups, generated pages,
# HTML worker state/fragments, subprocess captures, and atomic-write files.
#
# .tmp/ already covers all of these; the explicit names below are the belt to
# its braces, for the case where a build writes one into the repository root
# instead. The yy-html* globs deliberately also match the old yy-html3* names,
# so a deployment that has not yet self-updated cannot leak one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.tmp/
*.new.*
*.bak
yy.html
yy-html*.html
yy-html*-*.json
yy-html*/
yt-dlp.*.stdout
yt-dlp.*.stderr

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Download output. Disposable scratch, and never redistribute downloaded media.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
t/
UC*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent instructions — local to this machine, not part of the public repo.
# AGENTS.md describes the maintainer's corporate-managed setup (SSH key names,
# account names, internal go-links), which does not belong in a public repo.
# It was tracked previously, so untracking it only removes it from the tip;
# the old blobs stay reachable by SHA until GitHub GCs them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENTS.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent tooling artifacts. Written by the corporate-managed Claude plugins on
# the maintainer's machine, not by anything in this repo — a capture-session
# hook logs here when it decides whether to upload a session. It declines for
# this repo because the active GitHub login is personal, but the directory is
# LinkedIn tooling state either way and must never reach a public personal
# repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp
